summary:
- topic: SPHS Marching Band Recognition
  text: The South Portland High School Marching Band was celebrated for winning a
    gold medal and receiving a five-star rating at the Maine Band Directors Association
    state finals, with director Jen Fletcher highlighting their dedication and resilience.
- topic: FY26 Budget Projection
  text: Finance Director Abigail Ketchen presented the first end-of-year projection
    for FY26, indicating a potential deficit that is currently offset by a one-time
    geothermal energy tax credit. She warned that the district's fund balance is nearing
    depletion, necessitating careful financial planning for FY27 and beyond without
    this buffer.
- topic: South Portland Schools Education Foundation
  text: Rebecca Stern provided an update on the formation of the South Portland Schools
    Education Foundation, a non-profit organization aiming to raise funds for non-district
    associated costs. The committee is working towards establishing 501(c)(3) status
    and a board of directors by July 2026, leveraging community partners and pro bono
    legal assistance.
- topic: Middle School Field Remediation
  text: Michael Nalli detailed the findings from soil testing at the South Portland
    Middle School field, identifying issues like low organic matter, weeds, compaction,
    and nutrient deficiencies. He outlined a five-step remediation plan and expressed
    intent to seek cost recovery from the original contractor, while board members
    urged community pressure and swift action.
- topic: Union Contracts
  text: The FY2025-28 South Portland Teachers’ Association (SPTA) contract was ratified.
    Several public commenters, including SPTA and SPESPA representatives, expressed
    gratitude for the SPTA agreement and strongly advocated for the swift and equitable
    resolution of the SPESPA (Support Professionals) contract negotiations.
- topic: Policy Updates
  text: The Board approved Policy JJIF, concerning the management of concussions and
    other head injuries, after a second reading and incorporating additional language.
    A first read was also conducted for Policy IGDJ on co-curricular activities.
- topic: Board Member Recognition
  text: Outgoing board members Tandy Ratliff and Susan Rauscher were recognized and
    thanked by their colleagues for their service, leadership, and contributions to
    the school district.
